Arara Code: expose local PTY Host recovery hooks to extensions.

Why a patch: extension APIs do not expose PTY Host heartbeat failures, a local-only
restart, or a host round-trip check. The patch delegates the local failure and
status action to an extension command and exposes restart/latency commands.
Stale direct-port state is reset even before the first successful connection.
Diagnosis, consent, file repair and user messages remain in the extension.
Remote backends and non-Linux status actions retain their existing behavior.
